1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 d6 4. d4 Bd7 5. Nc3 Nge7 6. Bc4 Nxd4 7. Nxd4 exd4 8. Qxd4 Nc6 9. Qe3 Be7 10. O-O O-O 11. Nd5 Bf6 12. c3 Be6 13. f4 Bxd5 14. Bxd5 Qd7 15. Bd2 Rae8 16. Rae1 Bd8 17. Qg3 Kh8 18. Re2 Ne7 19. Bb3 f5 20. Rfe1 fxe4 21. Rxe4 Nf5 22. Qd3 Rxe4 23. Qxe4 Qc6 24. Qxc6 bxc6 25. Re4 c5 26. Bc2 Ne7 27. Ra4 Nc8 28. Kf2 c6 29. Ra6 Bb6 30. a4 c4+ 31. Kf3 Ne7 32. a5 Bc5 33. g3 Rb8 34. Bc1 Kg8 35. Ba4 Kf7 ({"} 35... Rc8 {would have given Black at least an equal game. White's imprisoned rook would perhaps not be easy to attack, but would have little future before it." (Wayte) But} 36. Be3 Bxe3 37. Kxe3 Rc7 38. Kd4 {is still winning (Stockfish)}) 36. Bxc6 Nxc6 37. Rxc6 Rb7 38. h4 {("and White won" Source: Daily News (London), 9 April 1894)} Ke6 39. Rc8 Rb5 40. Rc7 Kf6 41. g4 h6 42. g5+ hxg5 43. fxg5+ Kg6 44. Kg4 Kh7 45. h5 Kg8 46. g6 Rb8 47. Kg5 Re8 48. Bf4 Rd8 49. Be5 Be3+ 50. Bf4 Bc5 51. h6 gxh6+ 52. Kxh6 Bf2 53. Rg7+ Kh8 54. Rh7+ Kg8 55. g7 (55. Bg5 $1 {is quicker (Stockfish)}) 55... Kf7 56. Rh8 Rg8 57. Rxg8 Kxg8 58. Bxd6 (58. a6) 58... a6 59. Be5 Be3+ 60. Kg6 Bc1 61. Kf5 Bxb2 62. Ke4 Ba3 63. Kd5 Be7 64. Kxc4 Bd8 65. Kb4 Be7+ 66. Ka4 Bd8 67. c4 Be7 68. Bc3 Bd6 69. Bb4 Bc7 70. Bf8 Bd8 {Source: BCM, May 1894, p203} (70... Bd8 {"By moving only Bd8 and Bc7, it appears to us that Black had still chances of a draw, which would have been wanting if White had played as suggested in the last note. The White B is now badly placed for winning." (Wayte) Not really true: White still wins comfortably, e.g.} 71. c5 Bc7 72. c6 Bd8 73. Kb4 Bc7 74. Kc5 Bxa5 75. Kd6 Bb4+ 76. Kd7 {, etc.}) 1-0

